From e46e883a360826636808a8f9f90aaece5c4247e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 11:06:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: configs: enable Multi-Gen LRU for taimen_defconfig

CONFIG_LRU_GEN has no `default y` in mm/Kconfig, so plain olddefconfig
never turned it on for this device on either 6.0 or 6.18 -- it has
simply never been built. Both of its dependencies (MMU,
64BIT || !SPARSEMEM || SPARSEMEM_VMEMMAP) are trivially satisfied on
arm64, so there is no y -> m demotion risk from enabling it.

This device runs 3.6 GB of RAM behind 5.5 GB of zram(lz4) swap, which
is exactly the workload MGLRU targets: better reclaim quality under
memory pressure from more accurate page-age tracking. Also set
CONFIG_LRU_GEN_ENABLED=y so it is actually active at boot rather than
merely present, matching how the feature is normally shipped -- no
runtime `echo` to /sys/kernel/mm/lru_gen/enabled required.

Verified via `make taimen_defconfig` + scripts/diffconfig: both
symbols land as requested (plus the expected dependent
LRU_GEN_WALKS_MMU=y), no demotion of either symbol or anything they
touch.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/taimen_defconfig | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/taimen_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/taimen_defconfig
index 0718da287d6f..e93b101c8ebd 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/taimen_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/taimen_defconfig
@@ -831,6 +831,8 @@ CONFIG_THP_SWAP=y
 CONFIG_GENERIC_EARLY_IOREMAP=y
 # CONFIG_DEFERRED_STRUCT_PAGE_INIT is not set
 # CONFIG_IDLE_PAGE_TRACKING is not set
+CONFIG_LRU_GEN=y
+CONFIG_LRU_GEN_ENABLED=y
 CONFIG_ARCH_HAS_CACHE_LINE_SIZE=y
 CONFIG_ARCH_HAS_CURRENT_STACK_POINTER=y
 CONFIG_ARCH_HAS_PTE_DEVMAP=y
-- 
2.55.0

